# Pin this project to the PUBLIC npm registry.
#
# This file exists because of a real production failure. package-lock.json was
# first generated on a machine whose npm resolves through an Apple-internal
# proxy, so 48 of its entries were resolved to artifacts.apple.com and
# npm.apple.com. Those hosts do not exist outside the corporate network, so
# Netlify's install died with ENOTFOUND and the deploy failed — while the same
# lockfile installed perfectly on the machine that wrote it.
#
# A project-level .npmrc overrides the user-level one, so a regeneration here
# asks the public registry rather than inheriting whatever ~/.npmrc points at.
# Any auth lines in ~/.npmrc stay scoped to their own hosts and are unaffected.
#
# NOTE, because it matters if this happens again: this file was NOT enough on its
# own. On a machine behind the proxy, `npm install --package-lock-only` reported
# "up to date" and left the private URLs in place, because npm will not
# re-resolve a lockfile it considers satisfied. The 48 URLs were corrected by
# rewriting them in the repo (see the commit message), which is safe because
# every entry carries an `integrity` hash and `resolved` is only a fetch hint.
# If private URLs ever reappear, rewrite them again rather than trusting a
# regeneration done behind the proxy.
#
# Keep this file COMMITTED. It is part of what makes the lockfile reproducible
# off a corporate network, which is what both Netlify and
# .github/workflows/ci-cd.yml's `npm ci` depend on.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
